 "prompt": "Forecast the S&P 500 index level (close) as of December 31, 2027, and separately the probability that the index experiences a drawdown of 20% or more from any 2026-2027 peak before that date. Establish the baseline: current index level, trailing and forward P/E, 2024-2026 annual returns, and the current earnings-growth consensus. Research and weigh the principal drivers: Earnings growth path and AI-capex contribution breadth; valuation mean-reversion base rates at current multiples; Fed policy and recession probability; concentration risk in mega-cap tech; margin sensitivity to wages and tariffs; historical 2-year return distributions from similar starting valuations. Deliverables: 3-5 mutually exclusive scenarios with probabilities, a most-likely trajectory, and at least 10 binary forecasts with concrete thresholds, counts or dates, each with a probability and resolution criteria anchored to verifiable sources.",
